    "q14-q18 (group new_tools) cover the tradability, limit-price and market-cap tools of issue-433 §8.1 PR-C. Their expected values come from query_data only: the script may not call the tools under test, otherwise a wrong tool would grade itself correct. Limit prices are recomputed here from the raw previous close and the band (round_half_up to the tick, as src/research/price_limit.rs does); market cap is the raw close times the latest float_after on or before the day (integer shares, see src/sqlite_market/security.rs 'shares_unit'); q17 stores no price at all, it only asks whether the answer admits the status is unknown.",
    "Why these days: 2020-01-07 is a plain main-board trading day for sh.600519/sh.600000, far from the GEM rule change and from any code migration, and the risk-warning table has no interval for sh.600000 then, which is the documented 'unknown status' case (D-82 Q4). 2020-08-25 is the first full session of the GEM 20% band (effective 2020-08-24), where the limit rule does not depend on the ST status, so the expected limit price is knowable. q15 also fetches market.adjustment_events for the window and is skipped (skipped: precondition_not_met) if an ex-rights event falls between the previous close and the day: the tool answers ex_rights_unverified there (D-81), so no price can be expected.",
